# `structure::MotionResult`

The time history of a linear integration.

## Signature

```cpp
structure::MotionResult
```

## What It Does

The result of the linear `motion`. Every array has the leading batch axes of the frame and load, then the time axis.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `time` | The sample times, `[time]`. |  |
| `displacement` | Node displacements, `[..., time, node, 3]`. |  |
| `velocity` | Node velocities, `[..., time, node, 3]`. |  |
| `acceleration` | Node accelerations, `[..., time, node, 3]`. |  |
| `reaction` | Support force and moment, zero at free degrees of freedom, `[..., time, node, 3]`. |  |
| `kinetic` | Kinetic energy at each time, `[..., time]`. |  |
| `strain_energy` | Strain energy at each time, `[..., time]`. |  |
| `residual_norm` | Out-of-balance force of each step. |  |
| `converged` | One where the step converged. |  |
| `breakdown` | One where the step met a mechanism. |  |
| `iterations` | The largest iteration count among the structures at each step, `[time]`. |  |

## Returns

Returned by the linear `motion`.

## Errors

Reading a field does not integrate again.

## Interpretation and Use

For an undamped linear run with `spectral_radius` one, `kinetic + strain_energy - (work of the load)` is conserved.

